<pre class='metadata'>
Title: Missing Returns Should Be Ill-Formed
Group: WG21
Audience: EWGI
Shortname: Pnnnn
Revision: 0
Status: D
Date: 2024-12-18
Editor: Jeremy Rifkin, jeremy@rifkin.dev
Abstract: Flowing off the end of a non-void, non-main, and non-coroutine function is undefined behavior in C++. This is an easy footgun to run into in C++ and all major C++ compilers currently warn about missing returns. We propose making this ill-formed, instead requiring `std::unreachable()` to be used to explicitly mark unreachable code paths.
